<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ida of Bernicia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 559</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ida was the first known king of Bernicia in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxon-chronicle">Anglo-Saxon Chronicle</a> he began to reign in 547 and built the fortress of Bamburgh on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northumberland">Northumberland</a> coast, which became the dynasty's chief seat. Later kings of Bernicia and Northumbria, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria">Æthelfrith</a>, Oswald and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu</a>, traced their descent from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ida-of-bernicia.jpg" alt="Ida of Bernicia" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Speed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ida_-_John_Speed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
